# Set me up

Chat flow from a fresh clone to a working vault. Not a README. One question at a time. Always offer a default. Skip any step. End by running a thin morning brief.

Product Copilot (Jira, skills, MCP Google/Snowflake) is a **separate** repo. Point them at it if it is not already a second Cursor root. Do not clone their meetings or people from anyone else's vault.

## Step 0 — Frame

> I'll fill your context layer from calendar and a few questions, then run a first morning brief. About 20 minutes. Stop anytime — whatever we wrote still works.

## Step 1 — Tools

Check what responds. Do not dump a form.

| Tool | Used for | Required? |
|---|---|---|
| Meeting capture (Glean default; Granola legacy) | transcripts | yes for sync |
| Google Calendar | today | strongly recommended |
| Slack | next actions | recommended |
| Gmail | commitments | recommended |
| Atlassian | tickets — via Product Copilot | recommended |
| Snowflake | data — via Product Copilot | optional |

Write their capture choice into `99_System/meetings/sources.json` `active_source`. Missing capture or Calendar: give exact connect steps, then continue with a thinner system.

## Step 2 — Who they are

Calendar + Slack profile first, then confirm. Write `99_System/context/00-me.md`. Mark guesses `[inferred]`. Include Slack user id if you can see it.

## Step 3 — Org

Last 30 days of calendar: propose directs, leadership, working group. Confirm. Write `03-people.md` **and** `99_System/meetings/routing.json` (`directs`, `leaders`). Wrong routing dumps everything in Inbox.

## Step 4 — Portfolio and goals

Jira (if Copilot MCP is up) + meeting titles → `02-portfolio.md`. Then the one question you cannot infer: **what does success look like this quarter?** → `04-goals.md`. Set `Last reviewed` today.

## Step 5 — Vocabulary

Phenom-wide terms live in Product Copilot. Load that glossary if the other root is open. Ask what their area uses that the shared glossary is missing — queue `@team` in `_promotion-queue.md`.

## Step 6 — Voice

Recent Slack/email → propose `01-working-style.md`. Then: **how do you know when something is done?**

## Step 7 — Routines

Recommend **meeting sync + morning brief** only. EOD (`extras/eod/`) and GSD (`extras/gsd/`) stay off until those two survive two weeks.

## Step 8 — First brief

Run `.cursor/rules/Daily/morning-brief.mdc` on real data. It will be thin — say so. Point at context-gap questions as the compounding part.

## Step 9 — Hand off

- `morning brief` each weekday. Answer its questions.
- `sync meetings` after days with a lot of calls.
- `plan my week` on Friday or Monday.
- Friction: say so in the session; it logs.

Then stop.
